the kaiapoi south regeneration area of  approximately twenty eight hectares lies  between raven key and hilton street just  east of the town center and runs  parallel to the kaiapoi river and then  turning in a southerly direction along  courtney drive is bounded by the kaikan  ooey stream and the courtney stream from  just south of rotana fer if you're  traveling south along hilton street on  your left hand side the area has been  identified as suitable for business use  which could include vehicle parking or  yard based activities such as a plant  nursery or a car sales yard continuing  south along hilton street towards  courtney drive this has been identified  as a heritage and Myung a chi area  recognizing the cultural ecological and  amenity significance there is a proposal  which the council supports for joint  management of the area with NATO it  could be a couple of smaller strips  suitable for recreation and acting as  ecological linkage leading through the  m'hir KY area from hilton street towards  the kaiapoi river and further south  leading from courtney drive to and  alongside ncf park over on the  right-hand side of hilton street this  area has been identified as suitable for  rural uses however that would exclude  intensive farming further south and  alongside wider place would be a  suitable area for a new neighborhood  park please note that there are two  different roading options being  considered in the kaiapoi south area  details of these can be found on the  council website or at redzone planned  nzd we'd like your comments on these  regeneration area proposals for full  details of all the options outlined in  let's plan or to comment on the plan  visit the council website at Waimakariri  govt TN z or red zone planned NZ or pick  up a copy of the plan from any council  server center or library
 

